abstract: >
The Chess Multiverse Error & Evaluation Dataset (CMEED) is an
open-source chess research dataset containing engine-annotated
inaccuracies, mistakes, and blunders extracted from professional
and competitive chess broadcast games. Each record includes player
metadata, opening information, engine evaluations, evaluation
swings, clock information, move details, and fully reconstructed
board positions represented as FEN strings before and after the
error move. CMEED v1.0 contains 994,269 error records extracted
from games played between January 2026 and May 2026 and is designed
to support chess analytics, human error modeling, machine learning,
decision-making research, and large-scale statistical studies of
human chess performance.

